The dungeon has fountains and pools in many places. Perhaps some
levels could be home to underground streams or rivers. The main "use"
would be to substantially annoy Diggers for Victory, who would dig
down and subsequently soak themselves rather than falling through the
floor. ;)

What's more, digging pools might make for an excellent monster trap. A
player could play a drum of earthquake and drown nearby monsters by
uncovering all the streams on the level. Fleeing monsters could be
kept at bay via a geyser spouting in a corridor. All in all, digging
downward on a "hidden water" tile to create such terrain would be a
very good idea in some circumstances, with the nice balancing cost of
blanking scrolls/diluting potions.

And in Sporkhack's Gehennon, perhaps there are underground pools of
lava instead...

"You dig downward. A torrent of lava bursts into the pit! The lava
doesn't feel hot, but you're sinking fast!"

As for how to *find* such pools, may I mention divining rods? Perhaps
a wielded quarterstaff warns of water below, or "detect food" finds
water as well as food.


